From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koyu <me@koyu.space>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:10:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Add an updates page

After the network page, downloads and stages the latest system image
through rpm-ostree, with the download progress estimated like in
BlossomOS' Software Update KCM. When the next boot gets a new image,
it restarts into it right away; setup then starts again. Setup can go
on, or back, once the system is up to date, or when updating failed.

Without an internet connection the page is skipped. For that, pages
can now implement skipPage(), which the wizard asks right before their
turn, and InitialStartUtil tells whether NetworkManager is online.

The setup user may upgrade and restart without asking. In a preview
the download is simulated and nothing restarts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
